Council, while we wait on the election night reporting system to update, Councilman Kling asked me to explain this process.

30
00:05:56,000 --> 00:06:00,000
And I think it's important to understand provisional ballots.

31
00:06:00,000 --> 00:06:07,000
If they are accepted, it means that they voted in the precinct and it needed further review by the Board of Registrars.

32
00:06:07,000 --> 00:06:13,000
Oftentimes, someone may be at the wrong precinct and those are rejected.

33
00:06:13,000 --> 00:06:18,000
You must be in your correct precinct in order for your ballot to be cast.

34
00:06:18,000 --> 00:06:26,000
And also, you could be missing an ID and you have an opportunity at a later date to present that to the Board of Registrars.

35
00:06:26,000 --> 00:06:34,000
Also, if you vote absentee in my office, but because of mail or for whatever reason, your absentee ballot did not make it back in time.

36
00:06:34,000 --> 00:06:41,000
You still have an opportunity for your ballot to be cast by voting provisional in the precinct.

37
00:06:41,000 --> 00:06:52,000
And so we take time to work with the Board of Registrars to ensure that every vote counts and there is a thorough review before today's canvassing.

